#: fm1companion/ui/clean_check.py:25
msgid "Checks whether everything is in its place after many firmware switches. <b>Quick check:</b> read only over USB, without risk. <b>Dump check:</b> compares a full backup of the flash sector by sector with all packages the app knows."
msgstr ""

#: fm1companion/ui/clean_check.py:28
msgid "<b>Quick check</b> asks for identity and version, with Melodee 1.6 and later also the resource status (factory sounds, font, Bluetooth program): the firmware recomputes header and CRC-32 itself for this. It does not look into the rest of the flash.<br><br><b>Dump check</b> needs a 1 MiB full backup (e.g. “Emergency full backup” in stage 2 or “full-flash-before.bin” from the recovery folder). It checks the boot header, the firmware area, a truncated V16, leftovers of V16 in the data areas and the Melodee resources. In ROM boot mode it only reads – it never writes.<br><br><b>Clean up V16 leftovers</b> (expert mode, ROM boot mode, <b>untested on a real device</b>): erases selected single 4 KiB sectors in 0x93000–0xA8FFF – but only those that, according to a freshly read backup, still carry exactly V16 bytes, and only if the flash holds a known firmware with the V15 layout byte for byte (Melodee, V15, SLOOP …), never with V16. Nothing is written. Beforehand the whole flash is read twice and backed up, checked after every sector, and the whole flash compared at the end; a journal makes an aborted run resumable. From everything known so far (emulator, source code), the leftovers are harmless – so leaving them is fine too."
msgstr ""

